{"title":"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the smallest positive integer that is neither prime nor square and that has no prime factor less than 50?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa61998608ac1e057fa9466a5c982b959fdf0c99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\hspace{.05in}3127\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\hspace{.05in}3133\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\hspace{.05in}3137\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\hspace{.05in}3139\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\hspace{.05in}3149$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"490\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The problem states that the answer cannot be a perfect square or have prime factors less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the answer will be the product of at least two different primes greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. The two smallest primes greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba318f7385187c693cb1859d9b4b1b587e649d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$53$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/e/afe61e5b80572ad5a200a0d9cd354ce12a8c7800.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$59$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Multiplying these two primes, we obtain the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/f/45f2c0503ed0e418c14df4964c6b6a777eaf4acc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3127$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />, which is also the smallest number on the list of answer choices. \n</p><p>So we are done, and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/3/3137694ab63b206b314e3483384f2462248e5746.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3127}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"83\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HISL2-N5NVg?t=526\">https://youtu.be/HISL2-N5NVg?t=526</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14159\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/qBXOgsZlCg4\">https://youtu.be/qBXOgsZlCg4</a> ~WhyMath\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8\" title=\"2012 AMC 8\">2012 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2012\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/w